Z||000005||wkayl||09-12-2000||08:07 PM||||I recieved 1/2 hr notice after working for a company for 13 years.  Our company was bought out a year before and the put in their own manager (I was ast. mgr before buyout).  He had ben in the business for 1 1/2 years and was on the fast track, looking out only for himself.  We didn't see eye to eye.  After a year of this, I recieved the notice..After a cost analysis of blah blah blah the position of blah blah blah is no longer needed.  I ended up getting a job with the parent company (they were a franchise) at 50% more money and got all my seniority from the years there. <P>So look at this as a stepping stone.  I moved from Minn to Co. Lots warmer here, but I miss my ice fishing.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ozzy||09-12-2000||08:42 PM||||Thing to do hear Bastard is get an AK 47 and climb up on the roof when nobody is looking. Then wait untill....oh, hang on. You were not employed by the USPS were you?<P>I have only been fired once and it sucked. But looking back it was the best thing that could have happened. We get all comfy cosy in one place and never dare to venture beyond the horizon therefore never knowing whats out there for us. My peers call me gutsy 'cause I won't take too much crap from any employer and I will leave if something does not sit right with me. This has always led me to better opportunities without exception.<P>You will do just fine. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||10
Z||000007||Gokart||09-12-2000||10:30 PM||||Sorry that happened to you GT, but if I remember right from other posts you weren't too happy there anyway so everything happens for a reason....right? I like to think so <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Good luck. Marc.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||09-12-2000||10:42 PM||||9 out of 10 voices in my head say don't shoot.<P>Did you save your employee manual? Likely you have gounds to make a major stink. That kind of firing is usually a violation of stated company policies. I.E. they have to yell at you then write you up then fire you kind of thing. I doubt you have anything they could just dump you for.||||reg||8
Z||000009||Raydar||09-12-2000||10:53 PM||||GT, What a bunch of hairballs. <BR>I'm certain that something else will turn up, though. The newspapers and employment websites are just full of businesses looking for technology workers. From some of your previous posts, it sounded like you needed a change, anyway. <BR>What the he!!, move to Atlanta. We're up to our armpits in computer jobs!<P>As an aside... my company is doing a major blood-letting in October. Gonna be interesting. We made money "hand over fist", last year, and they're gonna drop like 100 people just to make a few people's stock price go up a couple bucks a share. <BR>There *is no* freaking conscience left in the corporate world. <P>Good luck. I know you'll do well.<P>Okay, I just reread your post. I think that the others are right. I believe that I'd at least look into filing a lawsuit. But wait until <I>after</I> you've got another job.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||09-12-2000||11:00 PM||||Let me be the first to come right out and say CONGRATULATIONS! Too many times, people cannot consciously walk away from something that is inhibiting their growth for the reason that it would be "irresponsible" to quit.  Obviously from earlier posts you hated this job, and I think subconsciouly you were looking for a way out. Now you got it.<P>So file for unemployment. Work on your resume. Stay home and look at Ricki Lake's plush booty for a week. You are now righteously unemployed, and they do not have the documentation to prove that it was a termination from gross misconduct. They can likely fight an unlawfultermination suit, but you WILL win your unemployment claim!<P>Eat a box of Little Debbie's on the couch with Ms. Lake for me.   <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||09-13-2000||12:28 AM||||It seems that your mental instability is directly related to your previous employer. That is a "job related stress disorder". You should be able to collect unemployment for a very long time for that one! If you could prove that you were fired for a "medical condition" you could burn their butts! That would be like firing a woman because she is pregnant or firing someone who is handicapped just because they they need a wheel chair ramp. Besides, who is not mentally unstable from time to time?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||09-13-2000||12:44 AM||||Another note- Why were they monitoring your e-mail? Recent court decisions about privacy and networks have brought up the 1935 National Labor Relations Act. The NAtional Labor Relations Board and the ACLU have gone to court for fired employees over this. Source: PC world magazine Sept 2000, page 62. Basically, "water cooler talk" is not grounds for dismissal according to this article.||||reg||1
